    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0282" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/7–745</note>
                <head>No. 131 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-07">July 7, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum of Conversation</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: British desire for the visit to London of one or more
                    of our representatives at the Big Three Meeting</p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#top #nowrap">Participants:</cell>
                        <cell>British Minister, Mr. John
                                Balfour;</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Acting Secretary, Mr. Grew
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>In the course of his conversation with me this morning Mr. Balfour of the British Embassy said his
                    Government hoped very much that one or more of our group which would attend the
                    forthcoming meeting of heads of government in Berlin might pass through London
                    so that there might be a preliminary discussion of various matters which would
                    come up at the main meeting. He realized that we would not wish to give any
                    impression to the Russians that we were ganging <pb facs="0283" n="151"
                        xml:id="pg151"/> up on them but he thought that if one or more of our lower
                    level experts could come to London in advance it would be very helpful.</p>
                <p>I replied that I thought the feeling in our group was opposed to such preliminary
                    talks but that I would look into the matter immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oseph</hi>] C.
                                G[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rew</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
